hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15450","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed me, Uthman ibn al-Saib, their freedman, narrated to me, from his father al-Saib, the freedman of Abu Mahdhurah, and from Umm Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Mahdhurah, that both of them heard it from Abu Mahdhurah. Abu Mahdhurah said: I went out among ten youths with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was the most hateful of people to us. So they gave the adhan, so we stood giving the adhan, mocking them. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me these youths. So he said: Give the adhan. So they gave the adhan, and I was one of them. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, this is the one whose voice I heard. Go and give the adhan for the people of Makkah. So he wiped over his forelock and said: Say: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, twice, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, twice. Then return and bear witness that there is no god but Allah, twice, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, twice. Come to prayer, come to prayer, come to success, come to success, twice. Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, there is no god but Allah. And when you give the adhan with the first of Fajr, say: Prayer is better than sleep, prayer is better than sleep. And when you make the iqamah, say it twice: The prayer has begun, the prayer has begun. Did you hear? He said: And Abu Mahdhurah would not cut his forelock nor part it, because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over it."
"15451","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Uthman ibn al-Saib informed me, from Umm Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Mahdhurah, from Abu Mahdhurah, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned to Hunayn, I went out tenth of ten, and he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, twice only. And Rawh also said: twice."
"15452","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Jafar, Abd al-Rahman said: he is not al-Farra, from Abu Salman, from Abu Mahdhurah, he said: I used to give the adhan in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Fajr prayer. So when I said: Come to success, I said: Prayer is better than sleep, prayer is better than sleep, the first adhan."
"15453","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Mahdhurah, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me the sunnah of the adhan. So he wiped the front of my head and said: Say: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, raising your voice with it. Then say: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, twice, lowering your voice with it. Then raise your voice: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, twice, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, twice. Come to prayer, come to prayer, come to success, come to success, twice. So if it is the Fajr prayer, say: Prayer is better than sleep, prayer is better than sleep, twice. Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, there is no god but Allah."
"15454","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Bakr, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Mahdhurah informed me that Abd Allah ibn Muhayriz informed him, and he was an orphan under the care of Abu Mahdhurah, Rawh said: Ibn Miyar, and Ibn Bakr did not say it, when he equipped him to Sham. He said: So I said to Abu Mahdhurah: O uncle, I am going out to Sham, and I fear I will be asked about your adhan. So he informed me that Abu Mahdhurah said to him: Yes, I went out among a group, and we were on part of the road of Hunayn, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from Hunayn. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met us on part of the road. So the muadhdhin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the adhan for prayer at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So we heard the voice of the muadhdhin while we were turned aside. So we shouted, imitating him and mocking him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the voice, so he sent to us until we stood before him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Which of you is the one whose voice I heard raised? So all the people pointed to me, and they spoke truly. So he sent all of them and kept me. So he said: Stand and give the adhan for prayer. So I stood, and there was nothing more hateful to me than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nor than what he commanded me. So I stood before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) himself dictated to me the adhan. So he said: Say: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Then he said to me: Return and extend your voice. Then he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Come to prayer, come to prayer, come to success, come to success. Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, there is no god but Allah. Then he called me when I completed the adhan, and gave me a purse in it something of silver. Then he placed his hand upon the forelock of Abu Mahdhurah, then passed it over his face twice, then twice over his hands, then over his liver, then the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached the navel of Abu Mahdhurah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah bless you. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, command me with the adhan in Makkah. So he said: I have commanded you with it. And everything of hatred for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went away, and that turned into love for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I came to Attab ibn Asid, the governor of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Makkah, and I gave the adhan with him for prayer by the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15455","And those of my family I met who met Abu Mahdhurah informed me of the like of what Abd Allah ibn Muhayriz informed me."
"15456","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Amir al-Ahwal narrated to us, Makhul narrated to me that Abd Allah ibn Muhayriz narrated to him that Abu Mahdhurah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught him the adhan as nineteen phrases and the iqamah as seventeen phrases. The adhan: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Come to prayer, come to prayer, come to success, come to success. Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, there is no god but Allah. And the iqamah two by two: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Come to prayer, come to prayer, come to success, come to success. The prayer has begun, the prayer has begun. Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, there is no god but Allah."
